## Release Checklist

**Naming conventions (MUST follow):**
- Git tag: `vX.Y.Z` (e.g. `v0.3`)
- Release name: `vX.Y.Z — <short descriptive title>`
- Commit message: `vX.Y.Z: <description>`
- Release notes file: `.github/release-notes.md` (edit this template before each release)

**Before releasing:**
1. [ ] All tests pass (`npm test`)
2. [ ] Build succeeds (`npm run build`)
3. [ ] `planning.md` is regenerated from latest source
4. [ ] `.github/release-notes.md` is updated with accurate notes
5. [ ] Working tree is clean (all changes committed)
6. [ ] On `main` branch, up to date with remote

**How to release (future agents):**
```bash
# Option A: Use the release script
bash scripts/release.sh 0.3

# Option B: Manual steps
npm test && npm run build
gh release create v0.3 \
  --title "v0.3 — <title>" \
  --notes-file .github/release-notes.md \
  planning.md
```

**After releasing:**
- Commit any updated release notes
- Push to main
